1. Software Architecture
System Architecture
The Smart Study Planner & Task Manager system follows a three-tier architecture, consisting of:
-Frontend (User Interface)
-Backend (Application Logic)
-Database (Data Storage)
These components work together to allow students to manage tasks, schedules, and progress efficiently.
System Flow
-Student (User) logs into the system using the Frontend (web interface).
-The Frontend sends requests (e.g., login, add task, view schedule) to the Backend server.
-The Backend processes the request, such as: Verifying user credentials in the database, Retrieving tasks assigned to the student, Saving new tasks or updates
-The Database stores and retrieves data, including: User information (name, email, password), Study tasks (title, deadline, status), Scheduling data (planned study sessions)
-The Backend sends the response back to the Frontend.
-The Frontend displays updated information to the student in real time.
Component Description
-Student interacts with the system through the web interface and performs actions like login, task creation, and progress tracking
Frontend (Web Application) : User interface built using HTML, CSS, JavaScript and Sends requests to backend and displays results, For example, when a student clicks “Add Task,” the frontend sends task information to the backend.
Backend (Application Server): Handles business logic, Processes user requests, Communicates with database
Database stores: User data, Tasks and Schedules. Users Database Role is to store user account information. it stores: User ID, Name, Email, Password (encrypted). Tasks Database Role is to store all study tasks created by students.
It stores: Task title, Description, Deadline, Completion status, Linked user ID. Schedule Database Role is to store scheduling and calendar-related information. it stores Planned study sessions, Assigned dates and Schedule records
